  "notes": [
    "klines_1d and mark_price_klines_1d both start 2020-08-11T00:00Z (first full daily candle after BTCUSD_PERP onboarding at 2020-08-10T07:00Z); index_price_klines_1d starts 2020-08-01T00:00Z because the BTCUSD index predates the perpetual listing (requested startTime was 1596240000000 = 2020-08-01). The 10 extra index rows (2020-08-01..2020-08-10) have no matching perp/mark rows.",
    "All three kline sets are contiguous daily series with exactly 86,400,000 ms spacing, no duplicates or gaps, and no OHLC violations. Their last row is the in-progress 2026-09-02 candle (fetched ~05:10 UTC), so its values are partial.",
    "funding_rate rows include the fields symbol, fundingTime, fundingRate, markPrice, rateType. markPrice is an empty string \"\" for the first 3533 rows (2020-08-10 through 2023-11-01T00:00Z) and populated from 2023-11-01T08:00Z onward (3107 rows). rateType is \"Regular\" on every row.",
    "fundingTime values carry small millisecond offsets from the exact 8h grid (max 94 ms; 3112 rows). Pagination used last fundingTime + 1 ms, so no rows were skipped or duplicated at page boundaries (verified by strict monotonicity of the concatenated series).",
    "funding_rate has one genuine gap: no settlement record at 2026-06-30T08:00Z (16 h between consecutive rows). Confirmed by a direct bounded re-query. Total rows 6640 vs 6641 expected on a perfect 8h grid. Data left unmodified.",
    "All funding rates lie within [-0.0075, 0.0075] (observed min -0.00300000 on the COIN-M cap side, max 0.00186012).",
    "exchangeInfo was small enough (35,676 bytes, 30 symbols) to save in full; no truncation, no BTCUSD_PERP-only extraction was needed.",
    "fundingInfo endpoint is available (HTTP OK) but returned an empty array [].",
    "server_time.json was captured at the start of the session (2026-09-02T05:09:06.431Z).",
    "Klines mark/index rows: the volume-type fields are \"0\" and the field at index 8 (numTrades position) holds the count of index/mark samples in the day (86400 for full days, fewer for the in-progress day), per Binance conventions for these endpoints; values kept verbatim.",
    "No numbers were reformatted, rounded, or cleaned; every page file is the raw response body text."
  ]
